// Memory-safety contract: all generated code that takes a raw pointer out of an
// AssemblyScript object (string, Array, Uint8Array, …) does so *only* after
// stashing the source into a named local. AS GC marks named locals as roots, so
// the source object survives any allocation that happens before the wasm import
// call. No explicit __pin / __unpin needed for the generated code paths.
//
// The return-area buffer below is single-instance and therefore NOT re-entrant:
// a host import must not synchronously re-enter through a callback that itself
// uses a multi-value-return import, or the outer call's result will be
// corrupted.

