// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Option<T>. `tag == 0` = none, `tag == 1` = some. Use Option.some(v) /
// Option.none<T>() for clarity. For "none", `value` is a default-constructed T
// (zero for primitives; for class types T, callers must pass an arbitrary
// instance because AS classes can't be left default-uninitialized).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

